 class on a randomly selected day" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible outcomes do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,…,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Continuous Random Variables Given in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a237df-49f8-5b9f-8ecb-4dad61e3770e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352588} {:answer/id #uuid "75860877-723f-5912-aa59-75bbaf84ea57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352600} {:answer/id #uuid "76a3d0b5-2215-5df0-ac94-5572cbf3adf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/